  "prefLabel": "Plc 1903.03 Applying for Initial Doula Certification",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1903.03 Applying for Initial Doula Certification. Any individual who meets the qualifications specified in Plc 1903.01 who wishes to be certified as a doula in New Hampshire shall apply by complying with Plc 304.01, subject to the following:\n\n(a) On or with the profession-specific supplement required by Plc 304.01(a)(2), the applicant shall provide the information and documentation required by Plc 1903.04 and Plc 1903.05;\n\n(b) No criminal background check shall be required; and\n\n(c) The fee shall be the application processing and licensing fee specified in Plc 1002.55, provided that an applicant who is applying as active military or a military spouse shall not pay the fee.\n\nSource. #14429, eff 1-16-26, EXPIRES 1-16-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1900.html"
